2 ' An executable made with BUILD contains the Engine1999 runtime: the Engine1999 Runtime Exception
3 ' (file LICENSE-EXCEPTION of Engine1999) applies if the runtime is unmodified and its notice stays
4 ' in the executable (it shows with the command line option --engine1999-about).
10 ' hiscore - keeps one number (the high score, the best height ...) in a small text file (a library: LOAD LIBRARY "hiscore").
20 '   HI=FN HS_LOAD("game.hi")    the number in the file; 0 if there is no such file or it holds nothing usable. A missing file is not an error (EXISTS tests for it).
30 '   CALL HS_SAVE("game.hi",HI)  writes the number to the file. A file error (a folder that can't be written) is raised as usual: a program that wants to ignore
40 '                               it traps it in its MAIN program, where RESUME <label> can continue: ON ERROR GOTO handler ... CALL HS_SAVE ... LABEL done ... ON ERROR OFF,
50 '                               with LABEL handler / RESUME done. (RESUME <label> inside a PROC or FUNC would land in a frame that the error has already taken apart.)
60 ' A name without a driver ("game.hi") lives in the program's own folder (the driver local:, ~/.local/share/<program>/): the file is safe there and needs no
70 ' permission. HS_LOAD falls back to a file of that name in the current directory, where older versions of the games kept it, so scores are not lost; without a
80 ' program name (typed in) local: is the current directory itself. A name with a driver ("mem:game.hi", "config:game.hi") is used as it is.
90 ' Both use the file channel #1: a program must not have a file open on it at that moment.
100 LIBRARY "hiscore","HS_"
110 FUNC HS_FILE$(F$)
115   LOCAL I,R$
120   R$="local:"+F$
125   FOR I=3 TO 17
130     IF MID$(F$,I,1)=":" THEN R$=F$
135   NEXT I
140   RETURN R$
145 END FUNC
150 FUNC HS_LOAD(F$)
160   LOCAL V,A$,N$
170   V=0
180   N$=FN HS_FILE$(F$)
190   IF NOT EXISTS(N$) THEN N$=F$
200   IF EXISTS(N$) THEN
210     OPEN N$ FOR INPUT AS #1
220     IF NOT EOF(1) THEN
230       LINE INPUT #1,A$
240       V=VAL(A$)
250     END IF
260     CLOSE #1
270   END IF
280   RETURN V
290 END FUNC
300 PROC HS_SAVE(F$,V)
305   LOCAL N$
308   N$=FN HS_FILE$(F$)
310   OPEN N$ FOR OUTPUT AS #1
320   PRINT #1,V
330   CLOSE #1
340 END PROC
